<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Rostock</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1419">1419</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of Rostock, founded in 1419 in the Hanseatic city of Rostock with papal approval, is one of the oldest universities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and the oldest in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a> region. In the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it drew students from across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a> and the Baltic, and after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> it became a stronghold of Lutheran orthodoxy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/university-of-rostock.jpg" alt="University of Rostock" width="320" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown author Vector: Lệ Xuân · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siegel_Universit%C3%A4t_Rostock_1419.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
